  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14272746/assets/3d75aee0e2e92b398fc2d0febb36615ec135d6b83234a2911c79c99a591312f3.png)\n\nA container has the shape of a right circular cone. The height of the container is $18\\,\\text{in}$ and the diameter at the top of the container is $12\\,\\text{in}.$ Water in the container is evaporating so that its depth, $h,$ is decreasing at a constant rate of $2\\,\\text{in/h}.$ Find the rate of the water volume decrease when the water depth is $9\\,\\text{in}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nHint: Assume that the rate of decrease is positive.\n\nThe water volume is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{3}/\\text{h}.$",
